1
00:00:08,021 --> 00:00:11,821
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

2
00:00:12,895 --> 00:00:16,881
Sayidina Yahyaعليه السلام was a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

3
00:00:17,941 --> 00:00:30,397
There's a Hadith(حديث) narrated by Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) and At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ) and Al-Nasa'i(النسائى), Ibn Habban(إبن حبَّان) and al Al Hakim(ألحَاكِم) and the Hadith(حديث) is Sahih(صحيح).

4
00:00:31,690 --> 00:00:34,904
I'll read the Hadith(حديث) and translate it, as we go through it.

5
00:00:35,424 --> 00:00:36,650
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

6
00:00:36,683 --> 00:00:45,228
إنَّ اللهَ أمر يحيى بنَ زكريا بخمسِ كلماتٍ أن يعملَ بهنَّ,وأن يأمرَ بني اسرائيلَ أن يعملوا بهنَّ

7
00:00:45,848 --> 00:00:56,762
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى commanded Yahya bin Zakariyya(يحيى بن زَكَرِيا) with five commandments to perform in his self, and to command Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) to perform.

8
00:00:58,588 --> 00:01:00,347
فكأنه أبطأَ بهنَّ

9
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:03,493
So it seems that, he delayed conveying the message.

10
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:10,812
So he received the five commandments from Allah, and he didn't hasten in conveying them.

11
00:01:11,666 --> 00:01:17,063
فأوحى اللهُ إلى عيسى : إما أن يُبلِّغَهنَّ أو تبَلِّغْهن

12
00:01:17,743 --> 00:01:25,032
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى revealed to Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام, that he either conveys them or you convey them.

13
00:01:26,392 --> 00:01:30,265
Because Yahya(يحيى) has received the order and until now, he didn't convey it.

14
00:01:30,745 --> 00:01:34,398
So Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام went to Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى).

15
00:01:34,831 --> 00:01:36,111
Eesa(عيسى) went to him and said;

16
00:01:36,651 --> 00:01:43,243
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given you five commandments, you either convey them or I'll convey them, myself.

17
00:01:44,194 --> 00:01:46,024
Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى) said;

18
00:01:46,531 --> 00:01:48,217
Oh spirit of Allah!

19
00:01:49,017 --> 00:01:52,668
And why did he call Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) the spirit of Allah; Roohullah(رُوحُ الله)?

20
00:01:53,155 --> 00:01:58,098
Because; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى calls him in Qur'an, that he is the spirit of Allah.

21
00:01:58,682 --> 00:02:02,301
And it means that, the Rooh(روح) of Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) was created by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

22
00:02:02,341 --> 00:02:10,386
It doesn't mean that, he's the actual spirit of Allah; it means that, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى created the spirit of Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام.

23
00:02:11,433 --> 00:02:20,772
He told him; Oh spirit of Allah! I'm afraid, that if you convey them; I will be punished, or the Earth would swallow me.

24
00:02:21,198 --> 00:02:24,638
It is very important to convey the message, especially when it's needed.

25
00:02:24,972 --> 00:02:26,165
And that's why, the Ulama(عُلَمَا) say;

26
00:02:26,185 --> 00:02:28,860
لا بجوز تأخير البيان عن اوقت الحاجة

27
00:02:29,321 --> 00:02:35,233
The scholars say; It is not allowed to delay conveying the message beyond the time, it's needed.

28
00:02:35,446 --> 00:02:36,255
So Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى) said;

29
00:02:36,295 --> 00:02:43,488
I'm afraid that, if you go and do it, and I don't do it myself; I would be punished, and Allah could even maybe make their swallow me.

30
00:02:43,914 --> 00:02:46,961
So he went forth, and decided to convey the message.

31
00:02:47,908 --> 00:02:55,350
فجمع يحيى بني إسرائيلَ في بيتِ المقدسِ حتى امتلأ المسجدُ فقعد على الشُّرُفاتِ

32
00:02:55,630 --> 00:02:58,895
Yahya(يحيى) gathered the children of Israel(اسرائيل) to Jerusalem.

33
00:02:59,275 --> 00:03:00,469
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

34
00:03:00,515 --> 00:03:01,409
حتى امتلأ المسجدُ

35
00:03:01,442 --> 00:03:02,979
Until, the Masjid(مسجد) was full.

36
00:03:03,912 --> 00:03:05,704
فقعد على الشُّرُفاتِ

37
00:03:06,297 --> 00:03:08,421
So, Yahya(يحيى) sat on a high place.

38
00:03:08,461 --> 00:03:13,095
Shurufat(شُرُفات); Ash-Shurufah(الشُّرُفَة) can mean; window, and it could also mean; a high place.

39
00:03:13,461 --> 00:03:15,933
So he sat on a high place, and speak to them.

40
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:19,060
فحمد اللهَ وأثنى عليه ثم قال

41
00:03:19,406 --> 00:03:21,974
So he praised Allah, and he thanked Him and he said;

42
00:03:22,354 --> 00:03:28,673
إنَّ اللهَ أمرني بخمسِ كلماتٍ أن أعملَ بهن وآمركُم أن تعملوا بهنَّ

43
00:03:28,873 --> 00:03:34,739
Allah has commanded me five things to perform myself, and you should perform.

44
00:03:35,285 --> 00:03:41,977
He said; Number one; you worship Allah, and you associate no Gods beside Him.

45
00:03:42,837 --> 00:03:48,890
And the analogy of someone who's worshipping a god besides Allah; is like one of you,

46
00:03:49,376 --> 00:03:57,202
who bought a slave; So you have a slave; And you paid for that with your money in gold or silver.

47
00:03:57,762 --> 00:04:00,265
And then you told that slave to work for you.

48
00:04:00,585 --> 00:04:08,230
So the slave would go and work and instead of giving you the harvest; he would go and give it to someone else.

49
00:04:08,770 --> 00:04:11,145
Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى) said; Who would accept that?

50
00:04:11,699 --> 00:04:19,914
And then he said; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Is the One, Who created you, and the One, Who's giving you; so you should worship no one but Him.

51
00:04:20,741 --> 00:04:24,430
Meaning that, we are the slaves of Allah; We are owned by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

52
00:04:25,312 --> 00:04:28,901
He's the One, Who created us; So we shouldn't worship anyone beside Him.

53
00:04:29,268 --> 00:04:32,308
And He is the One, Who's sustaining us; therefore we should thank Him.

54
00:04:33,501 --> 00:04:35,653
Because we are the slaves of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

55
00:04:37,147 --> 00:04:45,666
وأمرَكم بالصلاةِ ، وإذا قمتُم إلى الصلاة فلا تلتَفِتوا فإنَّ اللهَ عزَّ وجلَّ يُقبِلُ بوجهِه على لعبد ما لم يلتَفِتْ

56
00:04:46,139 --> 00:04:46,979
Number two;

57
00:04:47,339 --> 00:04:49,091
I command you to pray.

58
00:04:49,811 --> 00:04:54,903
And then he said; and when you stand to pray; don't turn your face around.

59
00:04:55,383 --> 00:04:57,917
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Is facing you.

60
00:04:58,630 --> 00:05:01,322
And as long as you're facing Him; Allah Will face you.

61
00:05:02,122 --> 00:05:05,362
And as soon as you turn your face away; Allah Will turn His face away from you.

62
00:05:06,109 --> 00:05:09,098
It's the common mistake; turning the eyes around in Salah(صلوة).

63
00:05:09,591 --> 00:05:11,645
And that is something unacceptable in Salah(صلوة).

64
00:05:12,178 --> 00:05:17,783
One should not stare around, and keep track of everyone, who's coming in and out, and what's going around.

65
00:05:18,256 --> 00:05:19,576
That distracts you from Salah(صلوة).

66
00:05:20,056 --> 00:05:23,212
And as soon as, you do that; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will turn His face away from you.

67
00:05:23,545 --> 00:05:27,125
One should stare at the place of Sujood(سجود) throughout Salah(صلوة).

68
00:05:27,398 --> 00:05:37,246
وأمرَكم بالصيامِ ، ومثلُ ذلك كمثل رجلٍ معه صُرَّةُ مسكٍ في عصابةٍ كلُّهم يجِدُ ريحَ المسكِ ،

69
00:05:37,573 --> 00:05:41,706
وإنَّ خلوفَ فَمِ الصائمِ أطيبُ عند اللهِ من ريح المسكِ

70
00:05:42,826 --> 00:05:45,392
And then he said; And I command you; to fast.

71
00:05:45,999 --> 00:05:55,080
And the analogy of that is like, someone walking with a sack of musk, and everyone is able to smell it.

72
00:05:56,006 --> 00:06:04,996
And then he said; The smell of the mouth of the person who is fasting, is better in the eyes of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى than the smell of musk.

73
00:06:05,403 --> 00:06:14,192
وأمرَكم بالصدقةِ ، ومثلُ ذلك كمثل رجلٍ أسَره العدوُّ فشدُّوا يدَيه إلى عُنُقِه وقدَّموا ليضربوا عُنُقَه

74
00:06:14,452 --> 00:06:17,731
فقال لهم : هل لكم أن أَفتديَ نفسي منكم ؟

75
00:06:17,937 --> 00:06:21,917
فجعل يفتدي نفسه منهم بالقليل والكثيرِ حتى فكَّ نفسَه

76
00:06:22,351 --> 00:06:26,170
And I command you to give Sadaqah(صدقة); charity.

77
00:06:26,603 --> 00:06:28,150
And then, he gave them an analogy.

78
00:06:28,370 --> 00:06:36,650
He said; the analogy of that, is like a man, who was captured by the enemy, and they tied his hands to his neck; he is hopeless.

79
00:06:37,297 --> 00:06:39,950
And they forwarded him to execution.

80
00:06:40,564 --> 00:06:42,944
So this man was tied up.

81
00:06:43,417 --> 00:06:51,620
He has no way to run around; no way to defend himself, because his hands are tied to his neck, and they forwarding him to chop his head.

82
00:06:52,813 --> 00:06:57,720
So this man during; what he's going towards death?

83
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:05,295
He's bargaining with them, to release him, and he's trying to ransom himself with money.

84
00:07:05,595 --> 00:07:10,329
So he's giving them money; he's giving them money; he's giving the money until, they released him.

85
00:07:11,529 --> 00:07:13,438
The meaning of this analogy is that;

86
00:07:14,318 --> 00:07:21,060
by Sadaqah(صدقة); by giving Sadaqah(صدقة), and continuously giving Sadaqah(صدقة); we are ransoming ourselves from hellfire.

87
00:07:21,686 --> 00:07:27,529
We might be in a hopeless case; hands tied to the neck; going towards the direction of hellfire.

88
00:07:27,916 --> 00:07:31,376
Gives Sadaqah(صدقة) throughout the way, until you die.

89
00:07:32,163 --> 00:07:35,863
And we ask Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to free ourselves from hellfire.

90
00:07:36,077 --> 00:07:42,657
Sadaqah(صدقة) is a way of; Itq Min Al-Nar(عتق من النّار); It's a way to free oneself from hellfire.

91
00:07:43,824 --> 00:07:47,224
So give; and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will give you more.

92
00:07:47,811 --> 00:07:54,652
وأمركم بذكر اللهِ كثيرًا ، ومثلُ ذلك كمثلِ رجلٍ طلبه العدوُّ سراعًا في أثَرِه

93
00:07:55,725 --> 00:08:02,441
فأتى حصنًا حصينًا فأحرز نفسَه فيه ، وإنَّ العبدَ أحصنُ ما يكون من الشيطانِ إذا كان في ذِكرِ اللهِ تعالى

94
00:08:03,268 --> 00:08:05,789
And I command you to remember Allah, and make Dhikr(ذكر).

95
00:08:06,643 --> 00:08:11,858
And the analogy of that; is like a man who is pursued by the enemy; they're pursuing him.

96
00:08:12,291 --> 00:08:17,068
So he finds a very protective fortress.

97
00:08:17,542 --> 00:08:19,690
So he goes in it, and he protects himself.

98
00:08:20,357 --> 00:08:24,288
So imagine! This man running away, and the enemy is pursuing him;

99
00:08:24,595 --> 00:08:30,839
And he finds this castle; this strong fort and he goes in, and he closes the door, and he's safe.

100
00:08:31,399 --> 00:08:32,864
And then, Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى) says;

101
00:08:33,104 --> 00:08:38,538
And you are in the safest place from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) when you are remembering the name of Allah.

102
00:08:39,538 --> 00:08:46,361
You are in the safest place, you are protected from Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ); when you remember the name of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

103
00:08:46,401 --> 00:08:48,548
So remember the name of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى frequently.

104
00:08:48,814 --> 00:08:50,975
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ ذِكْرًا كَثِيرًا۝

105
00:08:51,188 --> 00:08:53,634
Remember the name of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى a lot.

106
00:08:54,394 --> 00:08:58,043
These are the five commandments of Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى) and this is a Hadith(حديث).

107
00:08:58,603 --> 00:09:00,069
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

108
00:09:00,149 --> 00:09:01,687
وأنا آمرُكم بخمسٍ

109
00:09:01,761 --> 00:09:03,401
And I have five commands to give you.

110
00:09:04,267 --> 00:09:06,614
Rasool Allah ﷺ spoke about the five commandments of Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى).

111
00:09:06,827 --> 00:09:09,953
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to give, his five commands.

112
00:09:10,359 --> 00:09:13,666
وأنا آمرُكم بخمسٍ أمرني اللهُ بهنَّ ;

113
00:09:14,073 --> 00:09:15,082
الجماعةُ ،

114
00:09:15,202 --> 00:09:16,828
والسمعُ والطاعةُ ،

115
00:09:16,975 --> 00:09:17,775
والهجرةُ ،

116
00:09:17,942 --> 00:09:20,034
والجهادُ في سبيلِ اللهِ ،

117
00:09:20,401 --> 00:09:27,129
فإنه من فارق الجماعةَ قيدَ شِبرٍ فقد خلع ربقةَ الإسلامِ من عُنُقِه  إلا أن يراجعَ ، ،

118
00:09:27,513 --> 00:09:34,164
 ومن دعا بدعوةِ الجاهليةِ فهو من جثَاءِ جهنَّمَ ، وإن صام وزعم أنه مسلمٌ ،

119
00:09:34,430 --> 00:09:40,199
فادعو بدعوةِ اللهِ التي سماكم بها المسلمين المؤمنين عبادَ اللهِ

120
00:09:40,886 --> 00:09:43,239
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; And I command you five things.

121
00:09:43,459 --> 00:09:44,179
Number one;

122
00:09:44,392 --> 00:09:45,191
جماعةُ

123
00:09:45,885 --> 00:09:48,778
Be with the community; the community of the Muslims.

124
00:09:49,245 --> 00:09:56,084
And this means, that you stick to the Muslims who are going to support you on As-Sirat al-Mustaqeem(اَلصِّرَاطَ الْمُسْتَقِيْم).

125
00:09:57,151 --> 00:09:59,850
You need to be part of that community.

126
00:10:00,590 --> 00:10:01,823
والسمعُ والطاعةُ

127
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:04,049
And you listen, and you obey.

128
00:10:04,616 --> 00:10:13,304
You listen means; whenever the commands of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى are given; you listen attentively with intention to follow,

129
00:10:13,518 --> 00:10:17,290
not with the intention to argue against them, or to find a way out.

130
00:10:18,203 --> 00:10:19,910
You listen, and you obey.

131
00:10:20,170 --> 00:10:21,377
السمعُ والطاعةُ

132
00:10:21,677 --> 00:10:26,133
You hear the command of Allah, and you say; I obey and I accept.

133
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,147
والهجرةُ

134
00:10:28,733 --> 00:10:38,873
You make Hijrah(هجرة), and this is mansukh(منسوخ); this order is abrogated, because after the Fath Makkah(فتح مكه), there is no more Hijrah(هجرة).

135
00:10:39,446 --> 00:10:40,186
It is Jihad(جهاد).

136
00:10:41,366 --> 00:10:42,773
And then, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

137
00:10:43,053 --> 00:10:44,535
والجهادُ في سبيلِ اللهِ

138
00:10:44,775 --> 00:10:48,978
Al-Jihad(الجهاد) in the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, in the path of Allah.

139
00:10:49,018 --> 00:10:50,333
And then, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

140
00:10:50,746 --> 00:10:58,767
And whoever leaves the Jama'ah(جماعة); the Muslim community, a span of a hand; he has taken out Islam from his neck.

141
00:10:59,454 --> 00:11:02,290
You imagine! Islam as a collar; you have taken it out.

142
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:05,673
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Except if he comes back.

143
00:11:06,959 --> 00:11:17,735
And then he says; And whoever raises the banners, and the slogans, and the mottos of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة); then he will be in hellfire.

144
00:11:18,521 --> 00:11:26,849
Da'wah Al-Jahiliyyah(دَعْوَةالجَاهلِيَّة) is the nationalism, and Al-Asabiyya(العصبيه); the jealousy of nationalism and tribalism.

145
00:11:27,836 --> 00:11:30,983
Islam is now a new identity.

146
00:11:32,023 --> 00:11:33,424
It's a new identity for us.

147
00:11:34,184 --> 00:11:37,544
So Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Call them with their names,

148
00:11:37,864 --> 00:11:39,860
المسلمين المؤمنين عبادَ اللهِ

149
00:11:40,580 --> 00:11:46,429
Give them the identity of Muslims, and Mo'min(مؤمن); believers; the servants of Allah.

150
00:11:46,589 --> 00:11:47,356
That's who we are.

151
00:11:48,029 --> 00:11:48,443
We are;

152
00:11:48,463 --> 00:11:50,495
المسلمين المؤمنين عبادَ اللهِ

153
00:11:50,702 --> 00:11:53,690
And that's the identity; we are proud with.

154
00:11:53,877 --> 00:11:54,923
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

155
00:11:54,976 --> 00:12:03,482
Whoever brings up these banners of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة); these nationalisms or tribalism or wherever you're going to call them, or sectarianism is;

156
00:12:04,795 --> 00:12:06,089
جثَاءِ جهنَّمَ

157
00:12:06,115 --> 00:12:08,914
Will be part of whatever is dumped in hellfire.

158
00:12:09,861 --> 00:12:12,388
So it is a matter of faith.

159
00:12:12,448 --> 00:12:15,104
This gets into the central belief of;

160
00:12:15,124 --> 00:12:16,158
الولآوالبرآ

161
00:12:16,191 --> 00:12:26,622
That our loyalty goes to; the faithful and the believers, and we have nothing to do with the ones, who reject the message of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

162
00:12:26,982 --> 00:12:28,295
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

163
00:12:28,909 --> 00:12:47,432
وَإِذْ قَالَتِ الْمَلَائِكَةُ يَا مَرْيَمُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ اصْطَفَاكِ وَطَهَّرَكِ وَاصْطَفَاكِ عَلَىٰ نِسَاءِ الْعَالَمِينَ۝

164
00:12:47,978 --> 00:12:57,374
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; And remember, when the angel said; oh Maryam(مريم)! Verily Allah has chosen you.

165
00:12:59,054 --> 00:13:02,818
So Maryamعليهِ السلام was the chosen woman out of mankind.

166
00:13:04,245 --> 00:13:06,707
Among the woman it is Maryamعليهِ السلام.

167
00:13:07,941 --> 00:13:09,767
And the Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث).

168
00:13:09,907 --> 00:13:17,406
And this Hadith(حديث) is authentic, and it's been narrated in different forms in many books of Hadith(حديث).

169
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:21,346
But the summary of it is that, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

170
00:13:21,426 --> 00:13:22,973
خيرُ نساءِ العالمينَ أربعٌ

171
00:13:23,706 --> 00:13:26,179
The best of the woman of the world are four.

172
00:13:26,853 --> 00:13:27,799
And then, he said;

173
00:13:28,612 --> 00:13:36,681
مريم بنت عمران، وآسية ابنة مزاحم، وخديجة بنت خويلد، وفاطمة بنت محمد

174
00:13:37,634 --> 00:13:41,973
These are the four best women of the world.

175
00:13:43,340 --> 00:13:46,916
Now what is the ranking among them; Among these four?

176
00:13:47,416 --> 00:13:55,786
There is a Hadith(حديث) and that Hadith(حديث) says that the best of the woman are Maryam(مريم), Summa(ثُمَّ); and then;

177
00:13:56,159 --> 00:13:58,661
after Maryam(مريم); Fatimah binte Muhammad(فاطمه بنتِ محمدﷺ)

178
00:13:59,281 --> 00:13:59,828
then;

179
00:14:00,321 --> 00:14:01,121
Khadijah(خديجه),

180
00:14:01,435 --> 00:14:02,335
and then; Asiyah(آسيه).

181
00:14:03,221 --> 00:14:06,361
Now in terms of Maryam(مريم) being the best.

182
00:14:06,734 --> 00:14:10,241
This is something that, there's very little dispute about it.

183
00:14:10,668 --> 00:14:14,511
Because she has been mentioned in Qur'an that; she's the one who's chosen.

184
00:14:15,251 --> 00:14:21,088
And we notice something interesting; that these four women are related somehow to Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

185
00:14:21,421 --> 00:14:23,861
Two of them raised up a Nabi(نَبِي).

186
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:28,175
And these two were; Maryam(مريم), she raised up Eesa(عيسى),

187
00:14:28,302 --> 00:14:28,975
and who?

188
00:14:29,515 --> 00:14:31,535
Asiyah(آسيه), she raised up Musa(موسى).

189
00:14:31,555 --> 00:14:33,814
Even though, she's not his mother, but she's the one who raised him up.

190
00:14:34,354 --> 00:14:46,683
You can see that the, the nurturing, that the woman gives to the child, in bringing up the child, as a strong Muslim character can elevate the woman to the highest level.

191
00:14:47,517 --> 00:14:50,343
And then we have a wife of a Nabi(نَبِي), and that's Khadijah(خديجه).

192
00:14:50,850 --> 00:14:55,975
And finally we have a daughter of a Nabi(نَبِي) and that's Fatimah binte Muhammad(فاطمه بنتِ محمدﷺ).

193
00:14:57,942 --> 00:15:01,644
These are the best of the woman of the world.

194
00:15:02,311 --> 00:15:06,477
There are a few Ahadith(احاديث) but all of them are weak.

195
00:15:06,890 --> 00:15:08,510
There is doubt in their Sanad(سند).

196
00:15:09,117 --> 00:15:16,153
But keep in mind that you cannot use this as an evidence; it's just information that could be true or false that,

197
00:15:16,716 --> 00:15:22,705
Rasool Allah ﷺ will marry, Maryam(مريم) and Asiyah(آسيه) in Jannah(جنة).

198
00:15:23,325 --> 00:15:26,662
There are a few Ahadith(احاديث) mentioned; but as I said;

199
00:15:26,902 --> 00:15:27,749
فی اسانید ھا  نظر

200
00:15:27,774 --> 00:15:30,514
all of them have a doubtful Sanad(سند).

201
00:15:31,581 --> 00:15:35,393
Some of the scholars did adopt this opinion, and some of them said; we don't know.

202
00:15:35,840 --> 00:15:42,722
But I am mentioning it to you, as something that has been mentioned in the books of history, and Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) talks about it.

203
00:15:43,342 --> 00:15:53,461
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says that, the angels came to Maryam(مريم), and delivered to her the news that, she has been chosen by Allah.

204
00:15:54,194 --> 00:15:56,906
So this news was given to her by the angels.

205
00:15:57,313 --> 00:15:59,466
They descended on her and gave her this news.

206
00:15:59,679 --> 00:16:05,179
Now, this has let some of the scholars like; Ibn Hazm(ابن حزم) For example; to say that Maryam(مريم) was a Nabiya(نبيّا).

207
00:16:06,379 --> 00:16:11,515
Ibn Hazm(ابن حزم) said that, Maryam(مريم) is a prophet, because the angels descended on her.

208
00:16:11,829 --> 00:16:16,570
But this is not accepted by the scholars of the ummah(امة).

209
00:16:16,890 --> 00:16:17,190
Why?

210
00:16:17,217 --> 00:16:18,850
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in Qur'an;

211
00:16:18,890 --> 00:16:21,692
وَمَآ أَرْسَلْنَا قَبْلَكَ إِلَّا رِجَالًا نُّوحِىٓ إِلَيْهِمْ ۖ

212
00:16:21,966 --> 00:16:25,432
We have not sent before you, except men, whom We reveal to them.

213
00:16:25,745 --> 00:16:29,065
So the prophet-hood is among; Ar-Rijal(الرِّجال), is among the men.

214
00:16:29,792 --> 00:16:36,181
The fact that the angels came to Maryam(مريم); it doesn't mean that it was a Wahi(وحى) of revelation to her.

215
00:16:36,347 --> 00:16:42,170
But it was some sort of inspiration, or speaking of an angel to her, and it's a Karamah(كرامة).

216
00:16:42,436 --> 00:16:45,303
It's a Karamah(كرامة) from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to Maryam(مريم).

217
00:16:45,543 --> 00:16:46,538
وَطَهَّرَكِ

218
00:16:46,592 --> 00:16:48,938
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has purified you.

219
00:16:49,265 --> 00:16:51,305
وَاصْطَفَاكِ عَلَىٰ نِسَاءِ الْعَالَمِينَ۝

220
00:16:51,745 --> 00:16:54,884
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has chosen you above all the women of the world.

221
00:16:55,337 --> 00:17:00,270
And then the angels are conveying to her, the order of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

222
00:17:00,490 --> 00:17:10,065
يَا مَرْيَمُ اقْنُتِي لِرَبِّكِ وَاسْجُدِي وَارْكَعِي مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ۝

223
00:17:10,745 --> 00:17:11,849
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

224
00:17:11,883 --> 00:17:22,070
Oh Mary! Submit yourself with obedience to your Lord, and prostrate yourself, and bow down with the ones, who bow down.

225
00:17:22,310 --> 00:17:25,110
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; Uqnuti(اُقْنُتِي) from Qunoot(قُنُوت).

226
00:17:25,496 --> 00:17:30,805
Al-Qunoot(القُنُوت) is having Khushu'a(خُشُوعَ) to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and worshipping Allahسُبحانه وتعالى continuously.

227
00:17:31,752 --> 00:17:32,578
That's Qunoot(قُنُوت).

228
00:17:33,125 --> 00:17:33,632
And then;

229
00:17:33,698 --> 00:17:34,398
وَاسْجُدِي

230
00:17:34,638 --> 00:17:35,385
Sujood(سجود).

231
00:17:35,831 --> 00:17:37,148
وَارْكَعِي مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ۝

232
00:17:37,168 --> 00:17:37,801
And make Ruku'a(رُكُوْعَ).

233
00:17:37,861 --> 00:17:39,203
What is Sujood(سجود) and Ruku'a(رُكُوْعَ)?

234
00:17:40,383 --> 00:17:41,396
What does that refer to?

235
00:17:41,650 --> 00:17:42,456
It refers to Salah(صلوة).

236
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:47,992
It refers to Salah(صلوة); because as we said; Ruku'a(رُكُوْعَ) and Sujood(سجود) are the most prominent symbols of Salah(صلوة).

237
00:17:48,552 --> 00:17:51,171
If you see somebody in Ruku'a(رُكُوْعَ); you know that, that person is praying.

238
00:17:51,531 --> 00:17:54,291
If you see somebody in Sujood(سجود); you know that, that person is praying.

239
00:17:54,564 --> 00:17:57,906
So Ruku'a(رُكُوْعَ) and Sujood(سجود) are very prominent and unique positions of Salah(صلوة).

240
00:17:58,579 --> 00:18:01,906
That's why, they have been used to refer to Salah(صلوة) in Qur'an.

241
00:18:03,359 --> 00:18:04,765
وَارْكَعِي مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ۝

242
00:18:04,785 --> 00:18:08,092
Make Ruku'a(رُكُوْعَ) with the ones, who make Ruku'a(رُكُوْعَ); what is that referring to?

243
00:18:08,732 --> 00:18:09,712
Salat Al-Jama'ah(صلاة الجماعة);

244
00:18:09,892 --> 00:18:16,163
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is ordering Maryamعليهِ السلام to join in the Jama'ah(جماعة) and pray.

245
00:18:16,769 --> 00:18:19,244
ذَٰلِكَ مِنْ أَنبَاءِ الْغَيْبِ نُوحِيهِ إِلَيْكَ ۖ

246
00:18:19,671 --> 00:18:23,156
This is part of the news of the unseen, given to you.

247
00:18:23,616 --> 00:18:26,243
And this has been mentioned a few times in Quran.

248
00:18:26,436 --> 00:18:29,288
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى revealed to Muhammadﷺ the story.

249
00:18:29,622 --> 00:18:33,428
And within the story, or after the story, Allah would tell him; This was unseen.

250
00:18:33,542 --> 00:18:35,789
You didn't know it, and your people didn't know it.

251
00:18:37,089 --> 00:18:41,143
So it's a Ni'mah(نِعْمَة) from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى that He Has given to you, and it's a Ni'mah(نِعْمَة) on this ummah(امة).

252
00:18:41,168 --> 00:18:41,787
 Why?

253
00:18:42,694 --> 00:18:51,850
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! The stories of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) are such a wealth for us, in terms of guiding us to the right path.

254
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:59,117
All of this experience of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has been summarized for us in Qur'an.

255
00:18:59,284 --> 00:19:00,296
We have it, all with us.

256
00:19:00,569 --> 00:19:04,756
We have the long experience of all of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) throughout history.

257
00:19:04,962 --> 00:19:07,814
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has gathered all and put it for us in Qur'an.

258
00:19:09,207 --> 00:19:14,174
And this was something unknown to Muhammadﷺ, and it unknown to the people in his time.

259
00:19:14,560 --> 00:19:18,154
They barely; they barely knew about Musa(موسى) and Eesa(عيسى) by name.

260
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:24,793
And that's why, when Rasool Allah ﷺ met with the Christian servant in At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف).

261
00:19:25,919 --> 00:19:28,515
And Rasool Allah ﷺ asked him; where are you from?

262
00:19:29,262 --> 00:19:30,702
He said; I am from Ninowa(نينوی),

263
00:19:30,875 --> 00:19:31,782
Ninowa(نينوی) in Iraq.

264
00:19:32,075 --> 00:19:33,288
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

265
00:19:33,868 --> 00:19:35,535
You are from the town of;

266
00:19:35,575 --> 00:19:37,262
الرَّجُلَ الصّالِحِين يُوْنس اِبْن مَتَّى

267
00:19:37,588 --> 00:19:40,885
You are from the town of the righteous Yunus Ibn Matta(يونس ابن متّى).

268
00:19:41,192 --> 00:19:42,512
The man was surprised.

269
00:19:43,618 --> 00:19:47,724
Because people in Arabia; they don't know who Yunus Ibn Matta(يونس ابن متّى) was?

270
00:19:48,504 --> 00:19:51,177
As I said; they barely heard about Musa(موسى) and Eesa(عيسى).

271
00:19:52,397 --> 00:19:56,040
And now Muhammadﷺ is telling this man; Yunus Ibn Matta(يونس ابن متّى).

272
00:19:56,513 --> 00:19:57,440
He said; Do you know him?

273
00:19:57,520 --> 00:19:58,293
He was surprised.

274
00:19:58,347 --> 00:20:01,723
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Yes, he's my brother; we are Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

275
00:20:02,112 --> 00:20:04,345
These stories of Al-Ambiyaa(الأنبِيَاء); they were not known.

276
00:20:04,505 --> 00:20:08,480
And they are distorted in the Old Testament and the New Testament.

277
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:10,527
They don't exist in the pure form.

278
00:20:11,107 --> 00:20:14,672
So the only reference, the only reference for the stories of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) is Qur'an.

279
00:20:15,392 --> 00:20:18,098
And the interpretation given to it by Rasool Allah ﷺ in Hadith(حديث).

280
00:20:18,405 --> 00:20:19,612
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

281
00:20:19,845 --> 00:20:24,518
إِذْ قَالَتِ الْمَلَائِكَةُ يَا مَرْيَمُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُبَشِّرُكِ بِكَلِمَةٍ مِّنْهُ

282
00:20:24,791 --> 00:20:32,221
And remember! When the angel said; Oh Maryam(مريم)! Verily, Allah gives you the glad tidings of a word.

283
00:20:32,601 --> 00:20:35,830
We'll get back to these Ayaat(آيات); We'll move on to the Ayaat(آيات) from Surat Maryam(سورت مريم).

284
00:20:35,883 --> 00:20:37,270
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

285
00:20:37,390 --> 00:20:47,702
وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ مَرْيَمَ إِذِ انتَبَذَتْ مِنْ أَهْلِهَا مَكَانًا شَرْقِيًّا۝

286
00:20:48,375 --> 00:20:56,031
And mentioned in the book, Maryam(مريم); when she withdrew in seclusion from her family, to a place facing east.

287
00:20:56,571 --> 00:20:58,881
Maryam(مريم); where was she living?

288
00:20:59,207 --> 00:21:00,607
Bait Al-Maqdis(بيت المقدس) from Jerusalem.

289
00:21:00,834 --> 00:21:02,896
She went outside towards the east.

290
00:21:03,210 --> 00:21:04,836
فاتخذت من دونهم حجابا

291
00:21:04,890 --> 00:21:09,433
She plays the screen from them, meaning that, she was away from her people; she was alone.

292
00:21:10,246 --> 00:21:12,135
فَأَرْسَلْنَآ إِلَيْهَا رُوحَنَا

293
00:21:12,155 --> 00:21:14,955
We send to her; Our Rooh(روح).

294
00:21:15,881 --> 00:21:21,367
The word Rooh(روح) in Qur'an has been used for three different meanings.

295
00:21:22,647 --> 00:21:28,279
It means; our spirit, our soul, Ar-Rooh(الرّوح); that's one meaning.

296
00:21:28,919 --> 00:21:35,258
Second meaning is; Ar-Rooh Al-Qudus(الرّوح القدس), which is Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل عليه السلام), and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

297
00:21:35,558 --> 00:21:36,171
رُوحَنَا

298
00:21:36,578 --> 00:21:41,154
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; Has called him; My Rooh(روح); The Rooh(روح) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

299
00:21:41,548 --> 00:21:43,993
And it is referring to Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل).

300
00:21:45,460 --> 00:21:49,020
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) has been called the Rooh(روح) of Allah.

301
00:21:50,273 --> 00:21:54,412
Not to mean literally that he is the Rooh(روح) of Allah; he is created by Allah.

302
00:21:54,892 --> 00:21:59,456
But he was named Roohullah(رُوحُ الله), because he is the one, who carries the words of Allah.

303
00:22:00,623 --> 00:22:04,992
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل عليه السلام) is the one, who is carrying the words of Allah; Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) is the Angel of Wahi(وحى).

304
00:22:05,592 --> 00:22:11,214
Any revelation of Scripture that was revealed, was through Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل عليه السلام).

305
00:22:12,207 --> 00:22:17,766
At-Torah(توراة) was revealed by Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل); Al-Injeel(الانجيل) by Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل); and Al-Qur'an(القرآن) by Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل); Az-Zaboor(الزّبور) by Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل);

306
00:22:17,986 --> 00:22:19,206
he is the angel of Wahi(وحى).

307
00:22:20,046 --> 00:22:24,781
And Wahi(وحى) is the word of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; it's the word of Allah.

308
00:22:25,688 --> 00:22:37,494
Also Rooh(روح) has been mentioned in Qur'an to refer to either the soul of Adam(آدَم), or the soul of Eesa(عيسى).

309
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:40,007
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has;

310
00:22:40,254 --> 00:22:41,847
فنفخنا فيه من روحنا

311
00:22:42,820 --> 00:22:47,906
The soul of Adam(آدَم), and the soul of Eesa(عيسى) were called the soul of Allah; the spirit of Allah.

312
00:22:48,913 --> 00:22:58,285
Again; because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى created these two souls from the beginning, in a different form, than the natural way that we multiplied.

313
00:22:59,245 --> 00:23:03,065
The reproduction of the human being happens through a husband and wife.

314
00:23:03,378 --> 00:23:10,387
But with the case of Adam(آدَم); Adam(آدَم) was created without a father and a mother, and Eesa(عيسى) was created without a father.

315
00:23:11,274 --> 00:23:12,080
So over here;

316
00:23:12,227 --> 00:23:13,214
رُوحَنَا

317
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:14,773
Means; Jibreel عليه السلام.

318
00:23:15,520 --> 00:23:19,380
فَأَرْسَلْنَآ إِلَيْهَا رُوحَنَا فَتَمَثَّلَ لَهَا بَشَرًا سَوِيًّا۝

319
00:23:20,140 --> 00:23:23,096
He presented himself to her, in a human form.

320
00:23:24,616 --> 00:23:25,929
Now Maryam(مريم) is alone.

321
00:23:26,943 --> 00:23:30,383
And now she suddenly sees a man that made her nervous.

322
00:23:30,683 --> 00:23:42,136
قَالَتْ إِنِّىٓ أَعُوذُ بِٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ مِنكَ إِن كُنتَ تَقِيًّا۝

323
00:23:42,583 --> 00:23:48,853
She said; Verily I seek refuge with the Most Gracious Allah from you, if you do fear Allah.

324
00:23:49,399 --> 00:23:54,770
She's making a Dua(دُعَا) to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and in the same time she's begging the man.

325
00:23:55,837 --> 00:23:56,383
She said;

326
00:23:56,497 --> 00:23:57,770
أَعُوذُ بِٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ مِنكَ

327
00:23:57,903 --> 00:24:01,051
I seek refuge in Allah. So, she's asking Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

328
00:24:01,331 --> 00:24:03,364
And then she's begging him, saying;

329
00:24:03,604 --> 00:24:04,604
إِن كُنتَ تَقِيًّا۝

330
00:24:04,651 --> 00:24:07,586
If you have any fear of Allah, meaning; Stay away from me.

331
00:24:08,106 --> 00:24:10,526
It made her nervous to see this man, when she was alone.

332
00:24:10,766 --> 00:24:12,026
And this man was approaching her.

333
00:24:12,453 --> 00:24:13,133
He said;

334
00:24:13,373 --> 00:24:23,277
قَالَ إِنَّمَآ أَنَا۠ رَسُولُ رَبِّكِ لِأَهَبَ لَكِ غُلَٰمًا زَكِيًّا۝

335
00:24:23,691 --> 00:24:25,104
The Angel said; I am!

336
00:24:25,137 --> 00:24:28,097
And she doesn't know that this is the angel; she thinks that it's a human being.

337
00:24:28,317 --> 00:24:32,704
I am only a messenger from your Lord to announce to you the gift of a righteous son.

338
00:24:32,764 --> 00:24:34,578
And this even made it worse.

339
00:24:35,284 --> 00:24:36,338
She ask and said;

340
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:40,437
قَالَتْ أَنَّىٰ يَكُونُ لِي غُلَامٌ وَلَمْ يَمْسَسْنِي بَشَرٌ وَلَمْ أَكُ بَغِيًّا۝

341
00:24:41,183 --> 00:24:47,889
She said; How can I have a son when no man has touched me; nor am I unchaste?

342
00:24:48,422 --> 00:24:53,762
قَالَ كَذَٰلِكِ قَالَ رَبُّكِ هُوَ عَلَىَّ هَيِّنٌ ۖ

343
00:24:53,942 --> 00:24:59,231
He said; So it will be, your Lord said; That is easy for me.

344
00:24:59,551 --> 00:25:10,618
وَلِنَجْعَلَهُۥٓ ءَايَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَرَحْمَةً مِّنَّا ۚ وَكَانَ أَمْرًا مَّقْضِيًّا۝

345
00:25:10,849 --> 00:25:13,525
And We Will make him a sign for mankind.

346
00:25:13,698 --> 00:25:16,478
Eesa Ibn Maryamعليه السلام is a sign for mankind.

347
00:25:16,818 --> 00:25:23,797
And Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! The most amazing personality is Eesa Ibn Maryamعليه السلام.

348
00:25:24,277 --> 00:25:26,004
His birth was miraculous.

349
00:25:26,317 --> 00:25:27,897
It was an amazing birth.

350
00:25:28,477 --> 00:25:30,731
His miracles are amazing, giving life.

351
00:25:31,411 --> 00:25:35,297
The way he was elevated was amazing; It was a miracle in itself.

352
00:25:35,610 --> 00:25:38,203
The descending of Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) is a miracle.

353
00:25:39,050 --> 00:25:44,672
So his whole life, Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! is an intriguing and amazing life.

354
00:25:44,766 --> 00:25:49,739
And that's why, the personality of Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) is the most controversial.

355
00:25:51,519 --> 00:26:02,920
The three religions; Islam, Christianity, and Judaism; the pivotal point of dispute is on Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

356
00:26:04,113 --> 00:26:09,833
The difference between the three religions; the point of contention, is on the reality of Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

357
00:26:10,489 --> 00:26:14,569
The Jews say that he was not the Prophet of Allah, and he was an illegitimate son.

358
00:26:14,976 --> 00:26:18,981
They said; He is not a legitimate son; he was born out of Zina(زنا).

359
00:26:19,694 --> 00:26:20,680
That's what the Yahood(يهود) say

360
00:26:20,734 --> 00:26:27,392
and Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! It's interesting to see, how the Christians can fall prey to the Jews, when they know, that's what the Jew say about their Nabi(نَبِي).

361
00:26:27,922 --> 00:26:35,622
The Christian say that; No! Jesus was born from the Virgin Mary, and he is the son of Allah.

362
00:26:35,908 --> 00:26:37,873
تَعَالَىٰ عَمَّا يَقُولُونَ عُلُوًّا كَبِيرًا۝

363
00:26:38,220 --> 00:26:44,761
And then the Muslims come and say; Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) was born from the Virgin Mary,

364
00:26:45,014 --> 00:26:49,944
and he is the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and he is the Righteous; One of,

365
00:26:50,104 --> 00:26:51,384
الاولی عظم من الرسل

366
00:26:51,404 --> 00:26:53,712
The five best of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى;

367
00:26:53,879 --> 00:26:56,679
but Allahسُبحانه وتعالى does not have a partner, and Allah does not have a son.

368
00:26:57,466 --> 00:27:01,008
So the difference focuses on Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

369
00:27:01,594 --> 00:27:07,827
And because of this contention, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Will send him down again to solve it.

370
00:27:09,253 --> 00:27:18,574
Because of this dispute that arose, it is he; Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) who will come down at the end of time and solve this, once and for all.

371
00:27:20,554 --> 00:27:21,594
He will not accept Jizya(جِزية);

372
00:27:21,628 --> 00:27:23,068
ويقتل الخنزير

373
00:27:23,088 --> 00:27:24,614
And will kill the pig,

374
00:27:24,654 --> 00:27:25,467
فيكسر الصليب

375
00:27:25,487 --> 00:27:28,225
And he will break the cross; he'll put an end to this.

376
00:27:29,138 --> 00:27:31,792
وَلِنَجْعَلَهُۥٓ ءَايَةً لِّلنَّاسِ وَرَحْمَةً مِّنَّا ۚ

377
00:27:31,812 --> 00:27:33,532
And he is a mercy from Allah.

378
00:27:33,665 --> 00:27:35,045
وَكَانَ أَمْرًا مَّقْضِيًّا۝

379
00:27:35,078 --> 00:27:36,194
And it is already decreed.

380
00:27:36,434 --> 00:27:40,681
So Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) is telling here, this is something that cannot argue with; it's already done.

381
00:27:40,828 --> 00:27:46,975
The Angel Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل); he came to Maryam(مريم) and he blew into her;

382
00:27:47,188 --> 00:27:48,802
فَنَفَخْنَا فِیْهِ مِنْ رُّوْحِنَا۝

383
00:27:48,822 --> 00:27:53,654
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; So We blew into her from Our Soul.

384
00:27:53,960 --> 00:27:57,992
And Eesa(عيسى) was created by the Kalimah(كلمه); the word and that is, Kun(كن);

385
00:27:58,685 --> 00:27:59,819
Kun-Fayakun(كن فيكون).

386
00:28:00,125 --> 00:28:02,625
That's how Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) was created.

387
00:28:03,219 --> 00:28:04,278
So she became pregnant.

388
00:28:04,538 --> 00:28:10,906
فَحَمَلَتْهُ فَانْتَبَذَتْ بِهِ مَكَانًا قَصِيًّا۝

389
00:28:11,106 --> 00:28:14,438
And she withdrew with him to a far place.

390
00:28:14,918 --> 00:28:17,485
Far place is; Bayt-Lahm(بيت لحم).

391
00:28:17,765 --> 00:28:21,866
She was pregnant, and she went towards Bayt-Lahm(بيت لحم); Bethlehem.

392
00:28:22,393 --> 00:28:27,611
And it seems that her pregnancy was concealed, and no one knew about it.

393
00:28:28,344 --> 00:28:31,811
She was able to hide it, throughout her pregnancy; nobody knew that she was pregnant.

394
00:28:32,184 --> 00:28:37,256
And when she felt that her delivery is approaching; she left Jerusalem.

395
00:28:37,596 --> 00:28:47,513
And she just went out of Jerusalem and when she got towards Bayt-Lahm(بيت لحم); she started feeling the pain of delivery.

396
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:52,259
So she fell down under a palm tree.

397
00:28:53,259 --> 00:28:54,625
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

398
00:28:54,925 --> 00:28:57,674
فَأَجَاءَهَا الْمَخَاضُ إِلَى جِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ

399
00:28:58,101 --> 00:29:02,079
And the pains of childbirth drove her to the trunk of a date-Palm.

400
00:29:02,666 --> 00:29:06,726
And I want you to imagine now that you are over there;

401
00:29:07,220 --> 00:29:14,055
imagine the situation! Maryamعليهِ السلام has been hiding this pregnancy for nine months.

402
00:29:15,202 --> 00:29:20,759
That's difficult and now she's leaving out of her town alone with no help.

403
00:29:21,179 --> 00:29:26,199
And now she's feeling that pain and it drives her and she falls down under a palm tree.

404
00:29:26,706 --> 00:29:29,031
It was so difficult on her. She said;

405
00:29:29,378 --> 00:29:38,000
قَالَتْ يَا لَيْتَنِي مِتُّ قَبْلَ هَٰذَا وَكُنتُ نَسْيًا مَّنسِيًّا۝

406
00:29:38,353 --> 00:29:43,768
Would that I had died before this, and had been forgotten out of sight.

407
00:29:44,001 --> 00:29:46,254
I wish that I have died before this.

408
00:29:47,428 --> 00:29:48,923
Sayidatna Maryam(سيدتنا مريم) was Afeefah(عفيفه).

409
00:29:49,503 --> 00:29:51,123
She was chaste and righteous.

410
00:29:51,910 --> 00:29:54,753
And now she's going to deliver a child, and she has never been married.

411
00:29:55,213 --> 00:29:57,680
And she knows the tongues of the people.

412
00:29:57,933 --> 00:30:04,662
And she knows the harm, that they would cause her and her family; the righteous family of Al-Imran(آلعمران).

413
00:30:05,022 --> 00:30:08,793
It became so difficult on her; She said; I wish that I have never lived before this.

414
00:30:09,693 --> 00:30:14,113
And I wish that nobody has known me and I was forgotten; I didn't exist.

415
00:30:14,793 --> 00:30:19,772
In that moment of difficulty, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided her with the Sakinah(سكينة).

416
00:30:20,999 --> 00:30:28,568
When things got to the level, where it's unbearable for her anymore; then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى brought her comfort; Ar-Rahmah(اَلرَّحْمَة),

417
00:30:28,884 --> 00:30:30,307
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

418
00:30:30,473 --> 00:30:40,503
فَنَادَىٰهَا مِن تَحْتِهَآ أَلَّا تَحْزَنِى قَدْ جَعَلَ رَبُّكِ تَحْتَكِ سَرِيًّا۝

419
00:30:40,923 --> 00:30:42,442
She heard a voice from beneath her.

420
00:30:42,622 --> 00:30:44,849
The Mufassireen(مفسرين) says; its either Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) or Eesa(عيسى).

421
00:30:44,989 --> 00:30:46,156
And this voice told her;

422
00:30:46,176 --> 00:30:47,376
لَا تَحْزَنِى

423
00:30:47,736 --> 00:30:48,981
Do not grieve;

424
00:30:50,054 --> 00:30:52,081
قَدْ جَعَلَ رَبُّكِ تَحْتَكِ سَرِيًّا۝

425
00:30:52,314 --> 00:30:55,877
Your Lord Has provided a water stream under you.

426
00:30:56,117 --> 00:31:06,150
وَهُزِّي إِلَيْكِ بِجِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ تُسَاقِطْ عَلَيْكِ رُطَبًا جَنِيًّا۝

427
00:31:06,357 --> 00:31:13,669
And shake the trunk of the date palm towards you; and it will let fresh ripe dates fall upon you.

428
00:31:14,215 --> 00:31:17,572
Allah provided her with water, and Allah provided her with dates.

429
00:31:19,032 --> 00:31:22,006
And it's a miracle from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, that Allah provided her with this.

430
00:31:22,072 --> 00:31:27,138
A water stream was now suddenly flowing under her; she can reach it, with her hands.

431
00:31:27,378 --> 00:31:34,500
And then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; Shake the palm tree; fresh ripe dates will fall unto you.

432
00:31:34,700 --> 00:31:37,208
Now we learn from this some very important lessons.

433
00:31:37,928 --> 00:31:38,742
Number one;

434
00:31:39,022 --> 00:31:44,955
Maryamعليهِا السلام just delivered the child; is helpless; alone.

435
00:31:45,588 --> 00:31:54,523
And she is told by Eesa(عيسى) or by Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) to shake, not the branch of the palm tree, but to shake What?

436
00:31:54,923 --> 00:31:55,548
جِذْعِ

437
00:31:56,161 --> 00:31:57,801
The base of the palm tree.

438
00:31:58,688 --> 00:32:02,348
And all of you know palm trees, and know how solid it is.

439
00:32:02,719 --> 00:32:07,959
If a group of men surround it and try to shake it, at the base; it's impossible.

440
00:32:09,092 --> 00:32:13,861
So what's the point in Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Is telling Maryam(مريم); Shake the base of a palm tree.

441
00:32:14,221 --> 00:32:15,577
She's not gonna be able to shake it.

442
00:32:15,910 --> 00:32:19,721
She's not gonna be able to even move it, a fraction of an inch.

443
00:32:20,088 --> 00:32:22,361
Why is Allahسُبحانه وتعالى telling her to shake it?

444
00:32:23,708 --> 00:32:26,726
Make an effort, she has to do her part.

445
00:32:27,019 --> 00:32:31,437
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى could have made the dates fall on her without her shaking.

446
00:32:31,684 --> 00:32:37,249
Because it's not the shaking of a palm tree that will make the fruit fall down.

447
00:32:37,476 --> 00:32:39,023
It is a Karamah(كرامة) from Allah.

448
00:32:39,936 --> 00:32:44,602
If you put your hands on a palm tree; don't expect any dates to fall on you.

449
00:32:45,242 --> 00:32:46,708
It's the Karamah(كرامة) from Allah.

450
00:32:47,335 --> 00:32:51,764
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى could have made the dates fall down without her intervention.

451
00:32:52,237 --> 00:32:55,544
But the Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants her to do her part.

452
00:32:56,704 --> 00:32:58,186
And that's a very, very important lesson.

453
00:32:58,766 --> 00:33:02,039
If we want the victory of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; we have to do our part.

454
00:33:02,399 --> 00:33:03,773
You have to take the first step.

455
00:33:04,566 --> 00:33:06,849
اِنْ مَشَيْةُ اليَّ هَرْوَلْةُ اِلَيك

456
00:33:07,115 --> 00:33:12,085
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says in the Hadith(حديث) Al-Qudsi(ال قدسى); If you walk towards me; I will run towards you.

457
00:33:12,498 --> 00:33:13,718
But you have to take the first step.

458
00:33:14,271 --> 00:33:15,233
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

459
00:33:15,253 --> 00:33:17,606
وَٱلَّذِينَ ٱهْتَدَوْاْ زَادَهُمْ هُدًى

460
00:33:17,840 --> 00:33:21,125
The ones who seek guidance; they look for it, Allah Will give it to them.

461
00:33:22,165 --> 00:33:24,152
If you seek guidance; Allah Will give it to you.

462
00:33:24,539 --> 00:33:29,941
If you wait they're expecting things to come to you without any effort; nothing will happen.

463
00:33:30,168 --> 00:33:37,788
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى does not reward the person for their laziness, procrastination, and passiveness.

464
00:33:38,381 --> 00:33:40,773
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants us to do our part.

465
00:33:41,527 --> 00:33:47,679
So Maryamعليهِ السلام put her hand on the palm tree these fresh, ripe dates fell on her.

466
00:33:48,139 --> 00:33:56,533
We also learn from this in conjunction with the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ; that it's the best food for Al-Nufasaah(النفساه);

467
00:33:57,147 --> 00:33:59,776
The woman who just delivered; the best food for her is what?

468
00:34:00,069 --> 00:34:00,602
Dates.

469
00:34:01,782 --> 00:34:08,908
Dates is the best food for the woman who just delivered a child, and this is also confirmed in the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

470
00:34:09,335 --> 00:34:11,487
They used to give Al-Nufasaah(النفساه); dates.

471
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:16,140
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى provided her with water, and provided her with the;

472
00:34:16,620 --> 00:34:18,765
فَكُلِي وَاشْرَبِي وَقَرِّي عَيْنًا ۖ

473
00:34:18,852 --> 00:34:21,605
So eat and drink and be glad.

474
00:34:22,079 --> 00:34:24,548
Now, we'll go back to the Ayaat(آيات) from Surat Al-Imran(سورة آلعمران).

475
00:34:24,901 --> 00:34:30,980
The Angel Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل); when he came to give her the glad tidings that she will have a child.

476
00:34:31,720 --> 00:34:33,113
The angel told her;

477
00:34:33,366 --> 00:34:49,285
إِذْ قَالَتِ الْمَلَائِكَةُ يَا مَرْيَمُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُبَشِّرُكِ بِكَلِمَةٍ مِّنْهُ اسْمُهُ الْمَسِيحُ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ

478
00:34:50,325 --> 00:34:56,044
Allah gives you the glad tidings of a word.

479
00:34:57,317 --> 00:35:01,400
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gave him his name; Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

480
00:35:01,986 --> 00:35:08,675
So he was named by Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and he carried the name of his mother; Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

481
00:35:09,035 --> 00:35:09,669
And then Allah said;

482
00:35:09,689 --> 00:35:12,954
وَجِيهًا فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ وَمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِينَ۝

483
00:35:13,448 --> 00:35:20,270
Held in honour in this world and in the Hereafter, and will be one of those, who are near to Allah.

484
00:35:21,243 --> 00:35:23,423
Eesa(عيسى) is held in honour.

485
00:35:24,456 --> 00:35:26,883
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! Eesa(عيسى) is honoured so much by the Muslims.

486
00:35:27,250 --> 00:35:29,959
And the Muslims; we have so much love for Eesa(عيسى).

487
00:35:30,919 --> 00:35:34,671
And I think overall that, we have more love for Eesa(عيسى) than the Christians have.

488
00:35:35,778 --> 00:35:39,518
And when he comes down; this ummah(امة) would be service for him.

489
00:35:40,571 --> 00:35:44,825
And then in Akhirah(آخرة); also Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is holding Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) in honour.

490
00:35:45,112 --> 00:35:46,221
So he has Wajaha(وجاها).

491
00:35:46,401 --> 00:35:54,063
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given him Wajaha(وجاها); this high status of honour, plus Rasool Allah ﷺ loved him so much.

492
00:35:54,890 --> 00:35:55,410
 Why?

493
00:35:55,637 --> 00:36:00,355
In addition to him being a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; he was the closest one to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

494
00:36:01,368 --> 00:36:05,710
Rasool Allah ﷺ has mentioned in a few Ahadith(احاديث), that he loves him so much.

495
00:36:05,757 --> 00:36:06,097
Why?

496
00:36:06,117 --> 00:36:06,650
Because;

497
00:36:07,110 --> 00:36:08,383
ليسَ بيني وبينَه نبيٌّ

498
00:36:08,623 --> 00:36:12,861
There's no prophet between me and him; We are the closest together.

499
00:36:13,321 --> 00:36:14,741
And then the angel told her;

500
00:36:14,888 --> 00:36:24,903
وَيُكَلِّمُ النَّاسَ فِي الْمَهْدِ وَكَهْلًا وَمِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ۝

501
00:36:25,443 --> 00:36:30,982
He will speak to people in the cradle and in man-hood, and he would be one of the righteous.

502
00:36:31,022 --> 00:36:32,149
يُكَلِّمُ النَّاسَ فِي الْمَهْدِ

503
00:36:32,502 --> 00:36:33,729
In cradle; in infancy.

504
00:36:33,982 --> 00:36:34,876
What did he say?

505
00:36:35,229 --> 00:36:39,245
What was the first words that Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) pronounce when he was born?

506
00:36:39,518 --> 00:36:40,685
إِنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ

507
00:36:40,791 --> 00:36:41,885
I'm the servant of Allah.

508
00:36:43,725 --> 00:36:50,967
The first words that came out from the mouth of Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) when he was born; is that I am the servant of Allah; I'm the slave of Allah.

509
00:36:51,153 --> 00:36:52,442
إِنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ

510
00:36:52,722 --> 00:36:56,462
This has been crossed out from the books of the Christians.

511
00:36:57,402 --> 00:36:58,681
The first word that he said is;

512
00:36:58,748 --> 00:36:59,695
إِنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ

513
00:36:59,895 --> 00:37:03,923
So he speaks to people in cradle; fil mahadi(فِي الْمَهْدِ).

514
00:37:04,357 --> 00:37:05,043
وَكَهْلًا

515
00:37:05,250 --> 00:37:08,059
Kahlan(كهلًا); Al-Kuhula(الكهولا) is man-hood.

516
00:37:08,346 --> 00:37:17,234
This is defined as over 33 years old or over 40; difference of opinion on the linguistic meaning of the word; but it means in man-hood, in adult-hood.

517
00:37:17,681 --> 00:37:19,898
But you can find that all of them say, it's over 30 years old.

518
00:37:20,245 --> 00:37:21,182
That's Al-Kuhula(الكهولا).

519
00:37:21,976 --> 00:37:27,664
And it's interesting to note that some of the scholars have said; that when Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) comes down;

520
00:37:27,831 --> 00:37:35,610
because Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم); he was elevated alive at a pretty young age; early 30s.

521
00:37:36,657 --> 00:37:40,795
When he comes down, these scholars say that the first thing he will say is;

522
00:37:41,468 --> 00:37:43,761
إِنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ

523
00:37:43,820 --> 00:37:44,951
I'm the servant of Allah.

524
00:37:45,255 --> 00:37:50,247
The first word that came out from his mouth when he was in the cradle was; I'm the servant of Allah,

525
00:37:50,501 --> 00:37:57,765
and the first word that will come out of his mouth in man-hood when he comes down to this world is; I'm the servant of Allah.

526
00:37:58,005 --> 00:38:01,051
And they use that as an explanation to this Ayah(آية);

527
00:38:01,218 --> 00:38:04,131
وَيُكَلِّمُ النَّاسَ فِي الْمَهْدِ وَكَهْلًا

528
00:38:04,464 --> 00:38:07,169
He speaks to the people in cradle and in man-hood.

529
00:38:07,656 --> 00:38:17,595
وَيُعَلِّمُهُ ٱلْكِتَٰبَ وَٱلْحِكْمَةَ وَٱلتَّوْرَىٰةَ وَٱلْإِنجِيلَ۝

530
00:38:18,142 --> 00:38:20,537
Allah Will teach him the book and wisdom.

531
00:38:20,557 --> 00:38:21,417
What is wisdom?

532
00:38:21,837 --> 00:38:22,883
The Sunnah(سنة) of who?

533
00:38:23,903 --> 00:38:25,263
The Sunnah(سنة) of Eesa(عيسى).

534
00:38:26,169 --> 00:38:27,482
Every Nabi(نَبِي) has a Sunnah(سنة).

535
00:38:27,655 --> 00:38:30,189
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى taught him; Al-Injeel(الانجيل).

536
00:38:30,975 --> 00:38:35,131
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى taught him with Al-Injeel(الانجيل); the Sunnah(سنة) of Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

537
00:38:35,797 --> 00:38:37,691
وَرَسُولًا إِلَىٰ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ

538
00:38:37,871 --> 00:38:40,654
And a messenger to Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

539
00:38:41,240 --> 00:38:46,186
كَانَ الْاَنْبِيَاءَ يُبعَثُون إلى قومِهم خاصَّةً وبُعِثتُ إلى النَّاسِ عامَّةً

540
00:38:46,486 --> 00:38:52,625
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; The Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) were sent to there's people specifically; and I was sent to all of the world.

541
00:38:53,465 --> 00:38:56,005
 Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) here says; I was sent to Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

542
00:38:56,618 --> 00:39:00,140
All of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) had the local responsibility.

543
00:39:00,414 --> 00:39:03,634
Rasool Allah ﷺ; his responsibility was?

544
00:39:03,867 --> 00:39:05,673
To provide the message to the world.

545
00:39:06,199 --> 00:39:11,346
The Ayaat(آيات) in Qur'an, that presents Islam as a global message are about 20.

546
00:39:12,340 --> 00:39:17,977
There are about 20 Ayaat(آيات) in Qur'an, that say that Islam is a global religion, and a global message.

547
00:39:18,883 --> 00:39:20,817
18 of them are revealed in Makkah(مكه).

548
00:39:22,070 --> 00:39:27,493
So when Rasool Allah ﷺ was still in Makkah(مكه), and was still giving Da'wah(دعوة) only to the people of Makkah(مكه);

549
00:39:28,893 --> 00:39:33,390
Qur'an was already telling them that, this is a worldwide religion, and you were sent to all mankind.

550
00:39:33,683 --> 00:39:38,386
And an example of that is the Surat-ul-Qalam(سورةالقلم), which is one of the early Surah(سورة) revealed in Makkah(مكه);

551
00:39:38,566 --> 00:39:41,139
وَمَا هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعَالَمِينَ۝

552
00:39:41,406 --> 00:39:43,659
This is a reminder to all the world.

553
00:39:43,892 --> 00:39:46,575
Rasool Allah ﷺ was still giving Da'wah(دعوة) to the people of Makkah(مكه).

554
00:39:46,615 --> 00:39:49,061
But Allah Was telling him that, this is to all the world.

555
00:39:49,808 --> 00:39:53,690
So from the beginning; Islam was a worldwide religion.

556
00:39:54,290 --> 00:40:00,727
And most of the Ayaat(آيات) that presented Islam as a global message, were revealed in Makkah and not in Madinah(مَدِينَه).

557
00:40:01,135 --> 00:40:04,715
From the beginning; this was a worldwide religion.

558
00:40:05,682 --> 00:40:06,628
رَحْمَةً لِّلْعَالَمِينَ۝

559
00:40:06,675 --> 00:40:07,515
In surat-ul-Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء);

560
00:40:07,535 --> 00:40:09,205
وَمَا أَرْسَلْنَاكَ إِلَّا رَحْمَةً لِّلْعَالَمِينَ۝

561
00:40:09,348 --> 00:40:11,037
We Have sent you as mercy for mankind

562
00:40:11,070 --> 00:40:13,030
and this is an Ayah(آية) revealed in Makkah(مكه) also.

563
00:40:13,487 --> 00:40:15,787
أَنِّي قَدْ جِئْتُكُم بِآيَةٍ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ ۖ

564
00:40:15,827 --> 00:40:18,614
I have come to you with a sign from your Lord.

565
00:40:18,927 --> 00:40:19,694
Eesa(عيسى) said;

566
00:40:20,134 --> 00:40:31,386
أَنِّي أَخْلُقُ لَكُم مِّنَ الطِّينِ كَهَيْئَةِ الطَّيْرِ فَأَنفُخُ فِيهِ فَيَكُونُ طَيْرًا بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ ۖ

567
00:40:31,599 --> 00:40:32,324
Eesa(عيسى) said;

568
00:40:32,678 --> 00:40:42,234
I designed for you out of clay; a figure like that of a bird, and breath into it, and it becomes a bird by Allah's leave.

569
00:40:42,628 --> 00:40:51,368
 Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) would bring some clay, molded into the shape of a bird; he would breathe into it, and the bird would be alive.

570
00:40:52,704 --> 00:40:56,324
He had the ability to give life to the dead.

571
00:40:56,684 --> 00:40:57,520
And this was;

572
00:40:57,673 --> 00:40:58,573
بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ ۖ

573
00:40:58,606 --> 00:40:59,928
He says; By the will of Allah.

574
00:41:00,288 --> 00:41:06,775
وَأُبْرِئُ الْأَكْمَهَ وَالْأَبْرَصَ وَأُحْيِي الْمَوْتَىٰ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ ۖ

575
00:41:06,908 --> 00:41:12,640
And I heal him who was born blind, and the leper.

576
00:41:13,613 --> 00:41:15,522
وَأُحْيِي الْمَوْتَىٰ بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ ۖ

577
00:41:15,642 --> 00:41:18,708
And I bring the dead to live by Allah's leave.

578
00:41:18,902 --> 00:41:22,262
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! You can see the amazing miracles; Allah Was giving Eesa(عيسى).

579
00:41:22,408 --> 00:41:25,228
He would put his hand on the blind; he would see.

580
00:41:25,715 --> 00:41:28,757
He would put his hand on the person who would not speak; he would speak.

581
00:41:29,037 --> 00:41:32,064
He would put his hand on the dead; the dead would wake up alive.

582
00:41:32,344 --> 00:41:35,010
He would breathe into a bird; the bird would fly.

583
00:41:35,756 --> 00:41:39,443
See the amazing miracles, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Was giving Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

584
00:41:39,770 --> 00:41:43,665
وَأُنَبِّئُكُم بِمَا تَأْكُلُونَ وَمَا تَدَّخِرُونَ فِي بُيُوتِكُمْ ۚ

585
00:41:43,905 --> 00:41:45,679
And I inform you of what you eat.

586
00:41:45,859 --> 00:41:47,492
وَمَا تَدَّخِرُونَ فِي بُيُوتِكُمْ ۚ

587
00:41:47,725 --> 00:41:49,644
And I tell you, what you're hiding in your homes.

588
00:41:49,937 --> 00:41:52,857
إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَآيَةً لَّكُمْ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ۝

589
00:41:53,117 --> 00:41:55,956
Therein is a sign for you, if you believe.

590
00:41:56,070 --> 00:42:04,905
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! With all of these; unbelievable; Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! Amazing miracles, nevertheless, Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) did not believe.

591
00:42:06,078 --> 00:42:10,215
Healing in front of them, giving life to the dead, breathing in a bird,

592
00:42:10,609 --> 00:42:16,854
and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى equips every Nabi(نَبِي) with miracles that challenge the people and what they do best.

593
00:42:17,501 --> 00:42:20,301
The people of Egypt; what was their field of specialty?

594
00:42:20,394 --> 00:42:20,834
Magic.

595
00:42:21,154 --> 00:42:24,523
And the people of Egypt; they reached to the highest levels of magic.

596
00:42:25,076 --> 00:42:27,136
Maybe even more advanced than the magic of today.

597
00:42:28,376 --> 00:42:34,688
And the magicians held such highest status in the society, that they were considered to be the high class.

598
00:42:35,248 --> 00:42:39,050
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gave Musa(موسى) miracles to challenge them, and what they do best.

599
00:42:40,010 --> 00:42:44,303
He gave him the stick, and the hand to come out white and shiny.

600
00:42:44,956 --> 00:42:48,116
Miracles to challenge them, and what they think, they are the experts in.

601
00:42:49,396 --> 00:42:53,972
People in the time of Eesa(عيسى) used to be into the field of medicine and healing.

602
00:42:54,679 --> 00:42:58,546
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى gave Eesa(عيسى) miracles to challenge them, in what they do best.

603
00:42:58,772 --> 00:43:05,872
And there are not going to be able to bring similar miracles; not only in their time, but until the day of judgment.

604
00:43:06,232 --> 00:43:13,471
Even now, if we are able to cure the blind and the leper, it's never going to be in the way that Eesa(عيسى) did it.

605
00:43:14,031 --> 00:43:19,106
We might be able to cure some of the diseases that Eesa(عيسى) was curing; but it's never going to be the same way.

606
00:43:19,506 --> 00:43:22,519
Eesa(عيسى) would just put his hand over the blind, and he would see.

607
00:43:22,793 --> 00:43:25,752
He would put his hand over the mouth of the person who cannot speak, and he would speak.

608
00:43:26,139 --> 00:43:30,632
Put his hand over the person who was leprosy, and he would heal him.

609
00:43:31,332 --> 00:43:36,158
Never would the world be able to come up with a miracle, and that's why, it's a miracle; It's Muajza(معجزة).

610
00:43:36,318 --> 00:43:38,111
And what does the word Muajza(معجزة) mean in Arabic?

611
00:43:38,551 --> 00:43:39,414
Unability.

612
00:43:39,651 --> 00:43:45,337
You are challenging the people, and they will be unable to come up with something, to challenge it.

613
00:43:45,817 --> 00:43:46,930
That's the meaning of Ijaz(عجاز).

614
00:43:47,057 --> 00:43:51,223
So the Muajza(معجزة) would continue to be Muajza(معجزة), until the day of judgment.

615
00:43:51,796 --> 00:43:54,083
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) did not believe, with all of these miracles.

616
00:43:54,663 --> 00:43:57,428
وَمُصَدِّقًا لِّمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيَّ مِنَ التَّوْرَاةِ

617
00:43:57,562 --> 00:44:02,144
And I have come confirming that, which was before me in At-Torah(اتّوراة).

618
00:44:02,671 --> 00:44:06,034
This has not only been mentioned in Qur'an, but it's in the Bible too;

619
00:44:06,314 --> 00:44:08,674
Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) himself says;

620
00:44:08,894 --> 00:44:15,907
I have came to confirm the law of the Torah(توراة); dot by dot, jot by jot, letter by letter.

621
00:44:17,120 --> 00:44:22,863
In the New Testament; in the Bible of today, Eesa(عيسى) said;

622
00:44:22,923 --> 00:44:26,309
I have came to confirm the law of the Torah(توراة).

623
00:44:26,822 --> 00:44:31,527
And then Paul comes up and says; You do not have to follow the law,

624
00:44:32,320 --> 00:44:37,389
you do not have to keep up with the law of Torah(توراة), in fact, you have to leave it behind because that's not the religion.

625
00:44:37,796 --> 00:44:41,860
And they follow Paul, and they leave the word of Eesa(عيسى) which is in the Bible of today.

626
00:44:44,167 --> 00:44:49,119
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! And that's why; the true founder of Christianity of today is Paul; it's not Eesa(عيسى).

627
00:44:49,479 --> 00:44:52,175
This is not the religion of Eesa Ibn Maryamعليهِ السلام.

628
00:44:53,542 --> 00:45:04,004
Even Michael Hart in his book, the hundred greatest; he has given Paul a higher status than Eesa(عيسى), than Jesus.

629
00:45:04,804 --> 00:45:08,278
He said; because he has more influence on the religion of Christianity than Jesus does.

630
00:45:08,971 --> 00:45:15,455
The Christianity of today, is influenced more by Paul than it is by Eesaعليه السلام.

631
00:45:15,769 --> 00:45:20,051
But the influence of Eesaعليه السلام is not lost; the influence of Eesa(عيسى) is on us.

632
00:45:20,904 --> 00:45:23,124
We are the inheritors of the message of Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم).

633
00:45:23,970 --> 00:45:26,424
وَلِأُحِلَّ لَكُم بَعْضَ ٱلَّذِى حُرِّمَ عَلَيْكُمْ ۚ

634
00:45:26,664 --> 00:45:30,706
And to make lawful to you, part of that which was forbidden to you.

635
00:45:31,019 --> 00:45:34,628
There were some laws that were made specifically as a punishment for Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

636
00:45:35,835 --> 00:45:40,730
Because Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) used to ask too many questions to their Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), and were very stubborn;

637
00:45:40,890 --> 00:45:43,090
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى punish them by some laws.

638
00:45:43,137 --> 00:45:47,781
Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) came to relief them of these restrictions on them.

639
00:45:48,535 --> 00:45:52,906
By the way, the message of Eesa(عيسى) had a very strong spiritual dimension to it.

640
00:45:53,199 --> 00:45:58,355
Because, the Jews in the time of Eesa(عيسى); they have became very dry hearted and rigid.

641
00:45:59,035 --> 00:46:01,968
They compiled lists of laws to follow.

642
00:46:03,155 --> 00:46:06,501
We have to do this, we have to do this, we have to do this, don't do this, don't do this.

643
00:46:06,761 --> 00:46:10,983
They made a list of 660 laws, and they would go through them.

644
00:46:11,490 --> 00:46:15,116
They would just follow the law blindly; because the heart was dead.

645
00:46:15,490 --> 00:46:16,583
There was no spirituality.

646
00:46:16,870 --> 00:46:24,128
So, Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) came to shake their heart, and bring a revival to their hearts again.

647
00:46:24,334 --> 00:46:28,933
And that's why you find that Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) had a very strong position against Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

648
00:46:30,066 --> 00:46:32,032
Because, they were attached to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) too much.

649
00:46:32,332 --> 00:46:40,718
They needed somebody to draw them out, by presenting a very strong Anti-Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) message.

650
00:46:41,505 --> 00:46:44,908
Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم); lead a very simple life, he never got married.

651
00:46:45,335 --> 00:46:48,195
He was a true representation of Zuhd(زهد).

652
00:46:48,641 --> 00:46:52,144
Because the people were so much attached to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا); he had to bring them back.

653
00:46:52,224 --> 00:46:53,950
The message of Muhammadﷺ is different.

654
00:46:54,790 --> 00:47:03,127
Muhammadﷺ came as an individual that has a little bit of everything, and has the best of everything,

655
00:47:03,861 --> 00:47:09,200
and this is the balanced message, and this is the religion of Al-Wasat(وصت); the middle way.

656
00:47:09,493 --> 00:47:16,333
So the personality of Muhammadﷺ has the best of Eesa(عيسى); the best of Musa(موسى); the best of Yusuf(يوسُف);

657
00:47:16,600 --> 00:47:24,542
 the best of the best of Nuh(نوح); the best of Adam(آدَم); the best of all of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), was brought together in the personality of Muhammadﷺ.

658
00:47:24,689 --> 00:47:26,879
So the Zuhd(زهد) of Eesa(عيسى) was in Muhammadﷺ,

659
00:47:27,193 --> 00:47:29,513
the beauty of Yusuf(يوسُف) was in Muhammadﷺ,

660
00:47:29,713 --> 00:47:31,941
the strength of Adam(آدَم) was in Muhammadﷺ,

661
00:47:32,181 --> 00:47:36,008
the patience of Musaعليه السلام was in Muhammadﷺ,

662
00:47:36,341 --> 00:47:39,843
the persistence of Nuhعليه السلام was in Muhammadﷺ.

663
00:47:40,050 --> 00:47:44,937
So Allah brought the best of these qualities, and put them in one man, and that's Muhammad صلوات اللہ وسلام علیہ.

664
00:47:46,043 --> 00:47:47,077
And then he told them;

665
00:47:47,310 --> 00:47:51,405
إِنَّ اللَّهَ هُوَ رَبِّي وَرَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوهُ ۚ هَٰذَا صِرَاطٌ مُّسْتَقِيمٌ۝

666
00:47:51,825 --> 00:47:57,666
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Is my Lord and your Lord; so worship Him! This is the straight path.

667
00:47:57,832 --> 00:48:00,585
We'll go back to the Ayaat(آيات) of Surat Maryam(سورت مريم)

668
00:48:00,952 --> 00:48:06,530
and talk about the rest of the story of Maryam(مريم), when she delivered the Eesa Ibn Maryamعليه السلام.

669
00:48:07,030 --> 00:48:08,550
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told her;

670
00:48:08,857 --> 00:48:13,565
فَإِمَّا تَرَيِنَّ مِنَ الْبَشَرِ أَحَدًا فَقُولِي إِنِّي نَذَرْتُ لِلرَّحْمَنِ صَوْمًا

671
00:48:14,865 --> 00:48:18,283
Now Maryamعليهِ السلام has a child with her.

672
00:48:19,346 --> 00:48:28,414
And it's going to be very difficult for her to convince the people; that this is her child, and that; it is the word of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

673
00:48:29,267 --> 00:48:32,687
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told her; Don't speak! Don't speak! We'll take care of it.

674
00:48:33,627 --> 00:48:36,969
You don't have to argue on your behalf.

675
00:48:38,236 --> 00:48:40,519
If you see someone, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

676
00:48:41,212 --> 00:48:49,851
And if you see any human being say, verily! I have vowed a fast and to the most gracious, so I shall not speak to any human being, this day.

677
00:48:50,551 --> 00:48:52,154
Say that you're fasting from speaking.

678
00:48:53,227 --> 00:48:54,994
Because, what will she tell the people?

679
00:48:55,714 --> 00:48:59,655
She will tell them, an angel came to me and told me, they're not going to believe her.

680
00:49:00,942 --> 00:49:02,555
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told her don't speak.

681
00:49:03,309 --> 00:49:07,205
فَأَتَتْ بِهِ قَوْمَهَا تَحْمِلُهُ ۖ

682
00:49:07,685 --> 00:49:10,285
She came to her people carrying the child.

683
00:49:10,645 --> 00:49:11,952
Immediately they said;

684
00:49:12,139 --> 00:49:18,088
قَالُوا يَا مَرْيَمُ لَقَدْ جِئْتِ شَيْئًا فَرِيًّا۝

685
00:49:18,188 --> 00:49:22,913
They said; Oh Mary! Indeed you have brought a thing that is mighty.

686
00:49:23,040 --> 00:49:23,973
What have you done?

687
00:49:24,713 --> 00:49:25,386
And then they said;

688
00:49:25,600 --> 00:49:36,348
يَٰٓأُخْتَ هَٰرُونَ مَا كَانَ أَبُوكِ ٱمْرَأَ سَوْءٍۢ وَمَا كَانَتْ أُمُّكِ بَغِيًّا۝

689
00:49:36,695 --> 00:49:45,075
Oh sister of Haroon(هارون)! Your father was not a man, who used to commit adultery, nor your mother was an unchaste woman.

690
00:49:45,435 --> 00:49:46,335
What have you done?

691
00:49:46,615 --> 00:49:47,949
So they're already accusing her.

692
00:49:48,415 --> 00:49:54,507
They told her, your father was not a man who would commit Zina(زنا), and your mother was a chaste woman.

693
00:49:55,327 --> 00:49:56,534
What have you done?

694
00:49:57,427 --> 00:49:59,559
They refer to her mother and father.

695
00:50:00,226 --> 00:50:00,926
And they also said;

696
00:50:00,946 --> 00:50:01,679
يَٰٓأُخْتَ هَٰرُونَ

697
00:50:01,713 --> 00:50:02,759
Oh sister of Haroon(هارون)!

698
00:50:03,399 --> 00:50:04,226
Who's Haroon(هارون)?

699
00:50:04,866 --> 00:50:09,399
Haroon(هارون); by the way, the Jews in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ, they said;

700
00:50:09,439 --> 00:50:13,117
See, Rasool Allah ﷺ does not know what he's talking about.

701
00:50:13,141 --> 00:50:16,761
He's saying that, Maryam(مريم) is sister of Haroon(هارون), and between them are hundreds of years.

702
00:50:17,661 --> 00:50:18,497
So what does this mean;

703
00:50:18,544 --> 00:50:19,291
يَٰٓأُخْتَ هَٰرُونَ

704
00:50:19,311 --> 00:50:20,264
Oh sister of Haroon(هارون)!

705
00:50:20,664 --> 00:50:21,924
It has one of two meanings.

706
00:50:23,051 --> 00:50:28,913
One of them is that, she had a brother, whose name was Haroon(هارون).

707
00:50:31,662 --> 00:50:36,254
And when they said that, your father and your mother did not commit Zina(زنا);

708
00:50:36,807 --> 00:50:41,024
they completed the rest of the family by mentioning her brother, who was also a righteous man.

709
00:50:41,851 --> 00:50:45,037
In other words, they are telling her; all of your family are righteous, what's wrong with you.

710
00:50:45,571 --> 00:50:46,411
This is one meaning.

711
00:50:47,657 --> 00:50:52,444
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says; those people used to name their children according to the names of their Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

712
00:50:53,424 --> 00:50:54,711
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in a Hadith(حديث);

713
00:50:54,927 --> 00:50:56,614
کانو تسمعون باسماٗ ٗانبیائھم

714
00:50:56,824 --> 00:51:01,323
They used to name their children after their Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

715
00:51:01,550 --> 00:51:07,410
Therefore, it's also something recommended to do to name after the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

716
00:51:07,483 --> 00:51:11,403
Rasool Allah ﷺ named his son Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم), which is the father of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

717
00:51:12,117 --> 00:51:12,752
This is one meaning.

718
00:51:12,799 --> 00:51:19,583
Second meaning would be that, they were bringing up Haroon عليه السلام; the Nabi(نَبِي) Haroon(هارون).

719
00:51:20,436 --> 00:51:23,356
Because, Al-Imran(آلعمران) are from the descendants of Haroon(هارون).

720
00:51:23,770 --> 00:51:25,181
They are descendants of Dawood(داؤد).

721
00:51:25,448 --> 00:51:28,455
And Dawood(داؤد) was a descendant of Haroon(هارون).

722
00:51:29,168 --> 00:51:35,527
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put the prophet-hood in Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل), not in Musa(موسى), but in the lineage of Haroon(هارون).

723
00:51:36,420 --> 00:51:43,736
So in other words, they're bringing up the fact that you are from a righteous family; you are from the righteous family of Haroon(هارون).

724
00:51:44,776 --> 00:51:45,616
What are you doing?

725
00:51:45,769 --> 00:51:48,705
So you might ask the question; how come they said, sister of Haroon(هارون)?

726
00:51:49,078 --> 00:51:50,898
Why didn't they say, daughter of Haroon(هارون)?

727
00:51:51,718 --> 00:51:52,773
Well in Qur'an they says;

728
00:51:53,133 --> 00:51:54,086
أَخَی عَادٍ

729
00:51:55,246 --> 00:51:56,226
The brother of Aad(عاد).

730
00:51:56,519 --> 00:52:02,769
When you are part of a family; you are called brother of that family; In Arabic language, that's how you say it.

731
00:52:03,015 --> 00:52:07,097
So, Hud(هود) was in Qur'an, and it is referred to Hud(هود) as;

732
00:52:07,117 --> 00:52:07,977
أَخَی عَادٍ

733
00:52:08,297 --> 00:52:09,310
The brother of Aad(عاد).

734
00:52:09,743 --> 00:52:12,417
Even though, he was a descendant of Aad(عاد) from the people of Aad(عاد).

735
00:52:12,530 --> 00:52:15,808
So it would mean; you are from the righteous family of Haroon(هارون),

736
00:52:16,115 --> 00:52:19,008
your father and your mother don't commit Zina(زنا), what have you done?

737
00:52:19,808 --> 00:52:20,761
فَأَشَارَتْ إِلَيْهِ ۖ

738
00:52:20,894 --> 00:52:21,614
She didn't Speak.

739
00:52:22,041 --> 00:52:24,014
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told her; Don't speak!

740
00:52:24,388 --> 00:52:28,734
So, she pointed to the child telling them; he's going to respond.

741
00:52:29,081 --> 00:52:35,699
قَالُوا كَيْفَ نُكَلِّمُ مَن كَانَ فِي الْمَهْدِ صَبِيًّا۝

742
00:52:35,933 --> 00:52:39,279
How can we talk to a child, who is in the cradle?

743
00:52:39,813 --> 00:52:40,726
What's wrong with you?

744
00:52:41,126 --> 00:52:42,766
Because she was pointing to Eesa(عيسى).

745
00:52:42,959 --> 00:52:45,326
She is pointing to him, said; he's going to respond back to you.

746
00:52:46,059 --> 00:52:47,513
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى made him speak.

747
00:52:47,639 --> 00:52:49,174
إِنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ

748
00:52:49,268 --> 00:52:52,988
He said; I am the slave of Allah.

749
00:52:53,441 --> 00:53:01,299
قَالَ إِنِّي عَبْدُ اللَّهِ آتَانِيَ الْكِتَابَ وَجَعَلَنِي نَبِيًّا۝

750
00:53:01,446 --> 00:53:04,552
He Has given me the Scripture, and made me a prophet.

751
00:53:04,832 --> 00:53:15,360
وَجَعَلَنِي مُبَارَكًا أَيْنَ مَا كُنتُ وَأَوْصَانِي بِالصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ مَا دُمْتُ حَيًّا۝

752
00:53:16,240 --> 00:53:18,260
And He made me bless wherever I am.

753
00:53:18,867 --> 00:53:22,236
Wherever, Sayidina Eesa(سيدنا عيسى) is; blessing is following him.

754
00:53:22,609 --> 00:53:23,749
He is a blessed man.

755
00:53:24,342 --> 00:53:27,468
وَأَوْصَانِي بِالصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ مَا دُمْتُ حَيًّا۝

756
00:53:27,488 --> 00:53:31,921
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has enjoined on me Salah(صلوة) and Zaka'at(زكوة) as long as I live.

757
00:53:32,275 --> 00:53:36,270
So, Salah(صلوة) and Zaka'at(زكوة) are commandments that were given to the Umam(اُمَمْ) before

758
00:53:36,303 --> 00:53:43,392
the Ummah(امة) of Eesa(عيسى) and the Ummah(امة) of Musa(موسى) and all of the Umam(اُمَمْ) before; they used to make Salah(صلوة) and they used to give Zaka'at(زكوة).

759
00:53:43,658 --> 00:53:45,585
وَبَرًّۢا بِوَٰلِدَتِى

760
00:53:46,245 --> 00:53:47,994
And dutiful to my mother.

761
00:53:48,488 --> 00:53:50,428
وَلَمْ يَجْعَلْنِى جَبَّارًا شَقِيًّا۝

762
00:53:50,648 --> 00:53:54,083
And made me not arrogant unblessed.

763
00:53:54,443 --> 00:53:55,157
And then he said;

764
00:53:55,317 --> 00:54:03,029
وَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيَّ يَوْمَ وُلِدتُّ وَيَوْمَ أَمُوتُ وَيَوْمَ أُبْعَثُ حَيًّا۝

765
00:54:03,395 --> 00:54:06,938
To refresh your memory again; even though we just talked about it, I think last week.

766
00:54:07,371 --> 00:54:17,680
We said that the most critical moments, difficult moments on the human being, are the moments of transition between two different phases in your life.

767
00:54:18,840 --> 00:54:20,654
As human beings; we go through phases.

768
00:54:21,960 --> 00:54:25,426
We live in the womb, and that's one phase, for nine months.

769
00:54:26,506 --> 00:54:31,518
And then we go through a transition phase and that's delivery.

770
00:54:31,778 --> 00:54:34,031
And we come to another world.

771
00:54:34,345 --> 00:54:40,767
During that transition, when we are leaving from one world to another; the world of the womb to the world of the earth.

772
00:54:41,354 --> 00:54:44,972
That's a very difficult and nervous moment on us.

773
00:54:45,865 --> 00:54:48,225
So when we are born, what is the first reaction?

774
00:54:48,658 --> 00:54:49,545
We cry.

775
00:54:49,798 --> 00:54:54,503
Because we are going through this transition; we are going from the known to the unknown.

776
00:54:55,143 --> 00:54:58,625
We're going from the world we're familiar with, to the unfamiliar world.

777
00:54:59,099 --> 00:55:04,719
You leave from the warmth of the womb; to this vastness of this new world around you.

778
00:55:05,317 --> 00:55:07,071
So that's a difficult moment.

779
00:55:08,817 --> 00:55:13,700
And then we live in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا); we were unfamiliar with it, we became familiar.

780
00:55:14,014 --> 00:55:16,154
It was unknown; it became known.

781
00:55:17,094 --> 00:55:19,182
And unfortunately, we become too attached to it.

782
00:55:20,668 --> 00:55:27,887
And then, when it's time for us to leave this world to the other world; we go through a transition phase, and that is very difficult.

783
00:55:28,294 --> 00:55:30,207
And it's more difficult than the one, before.

784
00:55:31,054 --> 00:55:32,259
And this transition phase is;

785
00:55:32,352 --> 00:55:33,219
سَكَرَاتُ الْمَوْت

786
00:55:34,052 --> 00:55:35,045
The agony of death.

787
00:55:36,019 --> 00:55:42,667
And this agony of death is like a swing; you are going back and forth in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and out; Conscious and unconscious.

788
00:55:43,400 --> 00:55:46,398
Until you finally cross the line, that's it.

789
00:55:46,465 --> 00:55:50,485
You leave the Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) for good, and you are going into an unknown world.

790
00:55:50,578 --> 00:55:51,581
عَالَمُ الْبَرْزَخْ

791
00:55:52,147 --> 00:55:57,804
And this is very difficult, and you find people are in a state of shock when they're dying, and pain and agony.

792
00:55:58,121 --> 00:56:00,483
Because they're leaving the Duniyah(دُنِيَّا); they're so attached to.

793
00:56:00,693 --> 00:56:02,360
And that's why; we shouldn't be attached to Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

794
00:56:02,753 --> 00:56:07,044
They are leaving the Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) they're so attached to; to something; it's unknown.

795
00:56:07,591 --> 00:56:11,977
Sulaiman Ibn Abdul Maalik(سليمان ابن عبدالمالك) came to one of the scholars, I think it's Abu Hazam(ابو حازم).

796
00:56:12,724 --> 00:56:13,184
And he said;

797
00:56:13,204 --> 00:56:15,397
ما بالنا نكره الموت

798
00:56:15,724 --> 00:56:16,926
How come we hate death.

799
00:56:17,866 --> 00:56:19,020
Abu Hazam(ابو حازم) said;

800
00:56:19,560 --> 00:56:27,025
يانكم عمرتم دنياكم وخربتم آخرتكم فتكرهون خروجاً من العمران إلى الخراب

801
00:56:29,512 --> 00:56:34,980
Sulaiman Ibn Abdul Maalik(سليمان ابن عبدالمالك); the Khalifah(خليفه) of Bannu Umayyah(بَنُواُمَيَّة); very wealthy and rich;

802
00:56:35,347 --> 00:56:38,785
he came to the scholar Abu Hazam(ابو حازم), he told him;

803
00:56:38,810 --> 00:56:39,831
how come we hate death.?

804
00:56:40,498 --> 00:56:47,477
Abu Hazam(ابو حازم) told him; because you constructed your Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) and you destroyed your Akhirah(آخرة),

805
00:56:47,704 --> 00:56:51,257
so you hate to go from what is constructed to what is destroyed.

806
00:56:52,157 --> 00:56:57,175
You built and you established yourself in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), and you didn't build the house for you in Akhirah(آخرة); you didn't build anything.

807
00:56:57,482 --> 00:57:00,781
So you don't want to go from something that is established, to something that is not.

808
00:57:00,941 --> 00:57:04,607
That's why, we need to build our future in Akhirah(آخرة).

809
00:57:04,774 --> 00:57:06,101
That's what we should establish.

810
00:57:06,154 --> 00:57:08,508
Because, you're going to leave whatever you established in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

811
00:57:09,455 --> 00:57:11,741
In that transition phase, it's very difficult.

812
00:57:11,948 --> 00:57:12,728
سَكَرَاتُ الْمَوْت

813
00:57:13,201 --> 00:57:17,715
And then we enter into the grave, and we see hellfire, and we see Jannah(جنة).

814
00:57:18,855 --> 00:57:23,030
And then the Day of Judgment starts; so we go through another transition.

815
00:57:23,370 --> 00:57:27,610
And that is taking us from the world of the grave to the world of Akhirah(آخرة).

816
00:57:27,803 --> 00:57:29,469
And that is worst of all.

817
00:57:30,155 --> 00:57:31,255
That's the most difficult.

818
00:57:31,562 --> 00:57:40,126
Because, your grave pops up, and you crawl out of your grave, and you come out to the Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), and you see the world is shaking; earthquakes,

819
00:57:40,566 --> 00:57:44,079
the ocean is catching fire and exploding, mountains are bursting,

820
00:57:44,613 --> 00:57:51,031
the sky above your head is cracking, people are running around you, as if they're drunk, the sun is right over your head.

821
00:57:51,491 --> 00:57:54,271
And you know, the state of shock when you wake up from sleep.

822
00:57:54,618 --> 00:58:00,384
And there's something surprising happening around you, while you are waking up, from a deep sleep in your grave.

823
00:58:00,590 --> 00:58:04,166
And imagine the shock that you will go through, when you see; what's happening in Akhirah(آخرة).

824
00:58:04,932 --> 00:58:08,272
So that is a very unpleasant and difficult and unsecure moment.

825
00:58:08,592 --> 00:58:10,687
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says about Eesa(عيسى);

826
00:58:10,861 --> 00:58:19,770
And Salam(سلام); Peace be upon me; the day I was born, and the day I die, and the day I shall be raised alive.

827
00:58:20,150 --> 00:58:29,703
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Is giving me peace, and the most needed moment when I was born, and when I die, and when I'm raised up again.

828
00:58:30,556 --> 00:58:32,449
And we know that Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) did not die yet.

829
00:58:32,676 --> 00:58:35,629
And this is one of the indications of his coming back.

830
00:58:35,929 --> 00:58:43,662
ذَٰلِكَ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ ۚ قَوْلَ الْحَقِّ الَّذِي فِيهِ يَمْتَرُونَ۝

831
00:58:43,875 --> 00:58:49,422
Such as Eesa(عيسى); son of Maryam(مريم); it is a statement of truth which they doubt.

832
00:58:49,802 --> 00:58:52,224
This is the true Word of Eesa(عيسى).

833
00:58:52,490 --> 00:58:55,690
If you want to know the life of Eesa(عيسى); these are the Ayaat(آيات).

834
00:58:56,810 --> 00:59:06,872
When Ja'far Ibn Abi Talib(جَعْفَرْ ابن ابى طَالِب) was summoned to meet Al-Najashi(ال نجاشى); and Amr Bin Al Aas(عمرو بن العاص) made a Fitnah(فِتْنَه),

835
00:59:08,372 --> 00:59:12,444
and he went and said to Al-Najashi(النجاشى); Ask him, what they say about Eesa(عيسى)?

836
00:59:13,524 --> 00:59:21,303
So Al-Najashi(النجاشى) called Ja'far Ibn Abi Talib(جَعْفَرْ ابن ابى طَالِب), and he told him; what do you say about Jesus?

837
00:59:21,723 --> 00:59:25,182
Ja'far Abu Talib(جَعْفَرْ ابو طَالِب) read these Ayaat from Surat Maryam(سورة مريم).

838
00:59:26,422 --> 00:59:34,463
And it is said in the story that, tears were flowing from the eyes of Al-Najashi(النجاشى), and the eyes of the priests.

839
00:59:35,296 --> 00:59:40,702
 Because of the beautiful words in the description of the story of Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) in Surat Maryam(سورة مريم).

840
00:59:42,108 --> 00:59:45,901
Something that is unsurpassed in the New Testament.

841
00:59:46,621 --> 00:59:55,253
If you read; you will not find any description similar to the description and the beautiful story of Eesa Ibn Maryam(عيسى ابن مريم) mentioned in Surat Maryam(سورة مريم).

842
00:59:56,080 --> 00:59:57,760
And Al-Najashi(النجاشى) became Muslim.

843
00:59:58,467 --> 01:00:01,179
And he made his Islam secret and concealed.

844
01:00:01,393 --> 01:00:04,006
And when he died; because nobody prayed Jinazah(جِنَازَه) on him;

845
01:00:04,293 --> 01:00:07,695
Rasool Allah ﷺ made Jinazah(جِنَازَه) on him in Madinah(مَدِينَه).

846
01:00:08,268 --> 01:00:14,207
With Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام; his environment was very, very difficult.

847
01:00:14,747 --> 01:00:24,636
And Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام went through extremely severe situations in the short time that he spent in Da'wah(دعوة), and he was accused.

848
01:00:25,236 --> 01:00:32,856
And the problem is that, he was accused with things that are very, very difficult for a human being to accept.

849
01:00:33,129 --> 01:00:35,364
They accused his mother and they accused him.

850
01:00:35,711 --> 01:00:40,178
And you know the accusations, that the Jews raised against Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام.

851
01:00:40,511 --> 01:00:46,202
All of this was a test for the Sabr(صبر), and the patience of Sayidina Eesa عليه السلام.

852
01:00:48,349 --> 01:00:57,898
And all of these Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); Rasool Allah ﷺ learn from their lives, Sabr(صبر), and forbearance, and their qualities.

853
01:00:59,102 --> 01:01:03,328
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تسلیما کثیرا

